diff --git a/docs/release-notes/0.19.0.md b/docs/release-notes/0.19.0.md
index d7e43bfcf..bf6a8e645 100644
--- a/docs/release-notes/0.19.0.md
+++ b/docs/release-notes/0.19.0.md
@@ -5,11 +5,13 @@
 * Add ``dtype="bfloat16"`` to {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.harmony_integrate`, which keeps the cluster assignments in bfloat16 to save GPU memory and time; several batch keys or the ``fast`` correction fall back to float32 with a warning {pr}`829` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 * Add ``multi_gpu`` to {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.harmony_integrate` to run on several GPUs, with results bitwise identical to one GPU {pr}`830` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 * Add ``shuffle_chunk_size`` to {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.harmony_integrate`, the number of consecutive same-batch cells dealt into each update block (default ``8``) {pr}`829` {smaller}`S Dicks`
+* Match {meth}`~rapids_singlecell.ptg.GuideAssignment.assign_mixture_model` to pertpy's mixture model and parameters {pr}`852` {smaller}`L Heumos`
 
 ```{rubric} Performance
 ```
 * Speed up {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.harmony_integrate` and lower its peak GPU memory on large datasets, also for float64 or Fortran-ordered NumPy input; results stay bitwise reproducible, but seeded results differ from 0.18.1 {pr}`829` {smaller}`S Dicks`
 * {func}`~rapids_singlecell.pp.harmony_integrate` with several batch keys that have thousands of levels in total runs slower than in 0.18.1 {pr}`829` {smaller}`S Dicks`
+* Speed up {class}`~rapids_singlecell.ptg.GuideAssignment` with CUDA kernels that read CSR, CSC and dense counts in place; {meth}`~rapids_singlecell.ptg.GuideAssignment.assign_to_max_guide` no longer densifies sparse input {pr}`852` {smaller}`L Heumos & S Dicks`
 
 ```{rubric} Bug fixes
 ```
